/**
 * Easel prototype — DRAW: what Buddy actually sketches on the board, and in what order.
 *
 * The open question is not the whiteboard chrome, it is the *figure*. The live mock draws
 * a concept map: a labelled centre, four labelled boxes, lines between them. So does the
 * CONNECT artifact (notes, wikilinks, a graph) and, in silhouette, so does REMEMBER (rounded
 * rectangles carrying short text). Three features, one picture — a scan of the page reads
 * "boxes joined by lines" three times and learns nothing new on the second and third.
 *
 * Every direction below is Self-Reliance, and none of them is a node graph:
 *
 *   A — Marked-up line   · one sentence, read closely. Marks, not boxes.
 *   B — Quadrant         · a plot. Two axes, four corners, terms placed rather than linked.
 *   C — Derivation       · an argument worked down the board, with a step revised mid-draw.
 *   D — Iron string      · the metaphor drawn literally. A picture, barely any text.
 *   E — Two voices       · one divider, two columns, and the trade between them.
 *   F — Chapter map      · a route with stops. Linear, which no other visual on the page is.
 *
 * All six animate, because the sketch arriving stroke by stroke is the actual pitch — a
 * figure that only works as a finished image is not a candidate. The draw order is part of
 * each proposal and is written out beside it, so the sequence can be argued about without
 * watching it frame by frame. Every stroke carries pathLength="1", so a 40px tick and a
 * 500px axis take the same beat; the live mock's fixed stroke-dasharray of 600 is why its
 * short strokes currently snap while its long ones crawl.
 *
 * Each figure is shown twice: in the desktop drawing area (the chat rail eats ~26% on the
 * right, shown dashed) and at phone size, where the chat is hidden and the whole figure
 * scales down to ~310px tall. The phone frame is the real test — it is where a figure with
 * five lines of handwriting stops being readable.
 *
 * Throwaway. Nothing here is wired into the site.
 */

type Figure = {
  readonly key: string
  readonly name: string
  readonly desc: string
  readonly steps: readonly string[]
  readonly svg: string
}

